{% comment %}
  Carbon — stop horizontal page “wiggle” / sideways scroll on mobile (vertical scroll unchanged).

  Root cause (shopcarbon.com, Mar 2026 check):
  - The announcement bar marquee uses `.announcement-bar--inner.announcement-bar--marquee` with a very wide
    scrollWidth (duplicated text track). The inner wrapper has overflow:hidden, but PARENTS
    `.announcement-bar` and `.announcement-bar-section` used overflow-x: visible, so the document
    can still gain a few dozen px of horizontal scroll (e.g. 375px viewport → 408px scrollWidth).
  - Carousels / gallery slides that sit slightly off-screen can add to the same effect.

  Install:
  1) Shopify Admin → Online store → Themes → Edit code
  2) Snippets → Add snippet → name: carbon-overflow-x-fix → paste this file’s contents (or upload)
  3) In layout/theme.liquid, inside <head> (before </head>), add:
       {% render 'carbon-overflow-x-fix' %}

  Or paste the <style> block into theme base.css / custom CSS if you prefer not to use a snippet.

  Note: `overflow-x: hidden` on html/body does NOT remove vertical scrolling; overflow-y stays scrollable.
{% endcomment %}
<style id="carbon-overflow-x-fix">
  /* Clip horizontal bleed; vertical scrolling unchanged */
  html,
  body {
    overflow-x: hidden;
    max-width: 100%;
  }
  @supports (overflow: clip) {
    html,
    body {
      overflow-x: clip;
    }
  }
  /* Marquee parents (Archetype / similar themes) */
  .announcement-bar-section,
  shopify-section.announcement-bar-section,
  .announcement-bar {
    overflow-x: clip;
    max-width: 100%;
  }
  @supports not (overflow: clip) {
    .announcement-bar-section,
    shopify-section.announcement-bar-section,
    .announcement-bar {
      overflow-x: hidden;
    }
  }
</style>
